## f2 | always | F2, 1.3.2 "We conduct a critical capability assessment prior to the first external deployment of a new frontier AI model"
Rule 1. Every proposal must be preceded by a critical capability assessment, if both that proposal is classified as "first_deployment" and that proposal is frontier.
## f3 | RS7=E | F3, footnote 4 "A critical capability assessment may not be conducted for low-risk external deployments ... if the appropriate governance function determines the residual risk of such deployments to be acceptable"; an exception to f2
Rule 1. Every proposal need not be preceded by a critical capability assessment, if both that proposal is classified as "low_risk" and that proposal is classified as "governance_found_acceptable".
## f4-check-d | RS5=D | F4, 1.3.2: conditions (1) and (2) trigger the determination
Rule 1. Every proposal must be preceded by a determination of any substantial modification, if all of the following hold: (a) that proposal is subsequent; (b) both that proposal is classified as "new_capabilities" and that proposal is classified as "could_undermine_justification".
## f4-check-r | RS5=R | F4, 1.3.2: the determination for every subsequent version
Rule 1. Every proposal must be preceded by a determination of any substantial modification, if that proposal is subsequent.
## f4-further-r | RS5=R | F4, 1.3.2: conditions (1) and (2) make a further assessment required
Rule 1. Every proposal must be preceded by a further critical capability assessment, if all of the following hold: (a) that proposal is subsequent; (b) both that proposal is classified as "new_capabilities" and that proposal is classified as "could_undermine_justification".
## f5 | always | F5, 1.3.2 "we conduct material capability change assessments on various checkpoints upon the completion of a post-training run"
Rule 1. Every proposal must be followed by material capability change assessments on various checkpoints, if that proposal is classified as "post_training_run_completed".
## f6 | always | F6, 1.3.3 "When a model reaches an alert threshold for a CCL, we will assess the proximity of the model to the CCL and analyze the risk posed"
Rule 1. Every proposal must be followed by an assessment of proximity to each level with a risk analysis, if both that proposal approaches that level and that level is critical.
## f7-rra | always | F7, 1.3.4 "Models reaching TCLs or CCLs will be subject to residual risk assessments"
Rule 1. Every proposal must be subject to a residual risk assessment, if there is a level such that all of the following hold: (a) that proposal has reached that level; (b) either that level is tracked or that level is critical, or both.
## f7-sc | always | F7, 1.3.4 "For models reaching CCLs, the residual risk assessment will be informed by a supplemental safety case"
Rule 1. Every proposal must have its residual risk assessment informed by a safety case, if there is a level such that both that proposal has reached that level and that level is critical.
## f8 | always | F8, 1.3.5 bullet 1: no T/CCL reached, deemed acceptable (a classification)
Rule 1. Every proposal is acceptable, if it is not the case that there is a level such that that proposal has reached that level.
## f9-acc | always | F9, 1.3.5 bullet 2: the classification; DM only for external deployment (RS8, both readings)
Rule 1. Every proposal is acceptable, if there is a level such that all of the following hold: (a) both that proposal has reached that level and that level is misuse; (b) all of the following hold: (i) if that proposal is external, then that proposal mitigates that level; (ii) at least one of the following holds: (a) there is a measure such that both that level recommends that measure and that proposal applies that measure; (b) either that proposal is classified as "security_assessed_adequate" or that proposal is classified as "open_release_benefits_outweigh_risks", or both.
## f9-dm | RS1=G | F9, 1.3.5 bullet 2, DM-h as a gate: "This is required only for external deployment"
Rule 1. Every proposal must have mitigations make the residual risk of harm acceptable, if all of the following hold: (a) that proposal is external; (b) there is a level such that both that proposal has reached that level and that level is misuse.
## f9-sec | RS1=G | F9, 1.3.5 bullet 2, SEC as a gate
Rule 1. Every proposal must have security mitigations that reach the recommended security level, if there is a level such that both that proposal has reached that level and that level is misuse, unless either that proposal is classified as "security_assessed_adequate" or that proposal is classified as "open_release_benefits_outweigh_risks", or both.
## f9-rel | RS1=G & RS8=rel | F9, 1.3.5 bullet 2 "not internal deployment or further development" read as a release
Rule 1. Every proposal need not have mitigations make the residual risk of harm acceptable, if all of the following hold: (a) either that proposal is internal or that proposal is classified as "further_development", or both; (b) there is a level such that both that proposal has reached that level and that level is misuse.
## f10-acc | always | F10, 1.3.5 bullet 3: the classification; DM only for external and high-risk internal deployment
Rule 1. Every proposal is acceptable, if there is a level such that all of the following hold: (a) all of the following hold: (i) that proposal has reached that level; (ii) both that level is critical and that level is classified as "ml_rd_and_misalignment"; (b) all of the following hold: (i) if either that proposal is external or that proposal is classified as "high_risk", or both, then that proposal mitigates that level; (ii) at least one of the following holds: (a) there is a measure such that both that level recommends that measure and that proposal applies that measure; (b) either that proposal is classified as "security_assessed_adequate" or that proposal is classified as "open_release_benefits_outweigh_risks", or both.
## f10-dm-same | RS1=G & RS9=same | F10, 1.3.5 bullet 3, DM as a gate; RS9 same: one act with bullet 2
Rule 1. Every proposal must have mitigations make the residual risk of harm acceptable, if all of the following hold: (a) either that proposal is external or that proposal is classified as "high_risk", or both; (b) there is a level such that all of the following hold: (i) that proposal has reached that level; (ii) both that level is critical and that level is classified as "ml_rd_and_misalignment".
## f10-dm-diff | RS1=G & RS9=different | F10, 1.3.5 bullet 3, DM-s as a gate
Rule 1. Every proposal must have mitigations make the residual risk of severe harm acceptable, if all of the following hold: (a) either that proposal is external or that proposal is classified as "high_risk", or both; (b) there is a level such that all of the following hold: (i) that proposal has reached that level; (ii) both that level is critical and that level is classified as "ml_rd_and_misalignment".
## f10-sec | RS1=G | F10, 1.3.5 bullet 3, SEC as a gate
Rule 1. Every proposal must have security mitigations that reach the recommended security level, if there is a level such that all of the following hold: (a) that proposal has reached that level; (b) both that level is critical and that level is classified as "ml_rd_and_misalignment", unless either that proposal is classified as "security_assessed_adequate" or that proposal is classified as "open_release_benefits_outweigh_risks", or both.
## f10-rel-same | RS1=G & RS8=rel & RS9=same | F10, 1.3.5 bullet 3 "not further development" read as a release
Rule 1. Every proposal need not have mitigations make the residual risk of harm acceptable, if all of the following hold: (a) that proposal is classified as "further_development"; (b) there is a level such that all of the following hold: (i) that proposal has reached that level; (ii) both that level is critical and that level is classified as "ml_rd_and_misalignment".
## f10-rel-diff | RS1=G & RS8=rel & RS9=different | F10, 1.3.5 bullet 3 "not further development" read as a release
Rule 1. Every proposal need not have mitigations make the residual risk of severe harm acceptable, if all of the following hold: (a) that proposal is classified as "further_development"; (b) there is a level such that all of the following hold: (i) that proposal has reached that level; (ii) both that level is critical and that level is classified as "ml_rd_and_misalignment".
## f11-acc | always | F11, 1.3.5 bullet 4: the classification; DM only for external and high-risk internal deployment
Rule 1. Every proposal is acceptable, if there is a level such that all of the following hold: (a) all of the following hold: (i) that proposal has reached that level; (ii) both that level is tracked and that level is classified as "ml_rd_and_misalignment"; (b) all of the following hold: (i) if either that proposal is external or that proposal is classified as "high_risk", or both, then either that proposal mitigates that level or that proposal is classified as "unlikely_misalignment_propensities", or both; (ii) either that proposal is classified as "security_assessed_adequate" or that proposal is classified as "open_release_benefits_outweigh_risks", or both.
## f11-dm | RS1=G | F11, 1.3.5 bullet 4, DM-g as a gate
Rule 1. Every proposal must have mitigations make the residual risk of significant harm acceptable, if all of the following hold: (a) either that proposal is external or that proposal is classified as "high_risk", or both; (b) there is a level such that all of the following hold: (i) that proposal has reached that level; (ii) both that level is tracked and that level is classified as "ml_rd_and_misalignment", unless that proposal is classified as "unlikely_misalignment_propensities".
## f11-sec | RS1=G | F11, 1.3.5 bullet 4, SEC-t as a gate
Rule 1. Every proposal must have a level of security assessed as adequate, if there is a level such that all of the following hold: (a) that proposal has reached that level; (b) both that level is tracked and that level is classified as "ml_rd_and_misalignment", unless that proposal is classified as "open_release_benefits_outweigh_risks".
## f11-rel | RS1=G & RS8=rel | F11, 1.3.5 bullet 4 "not further development" read as a release
Rule 1. Every proposal need not have mitigations make the residual risk of significant harm acceptable, if all of the following hold: (a) that proposal is classified as "further_development"; (b) there is a level such that all of the following hold: (i) that proposal has reached that level; (ii) both that level is tracked and that level is classified as "ml_rd_and_misalignment".
## f12-p | RS2=P | F12, 2.1.2 step 2, within the process for models reaching a misuse T/CCL
Rule 1. Every proposal must not proceed, if all of the following hold: (a) that proposal is external; (b) there is a level such that both that proposal has reached that level and that level is misuse, unless that proposal is classified as "governance_found_acceptable".
## f12-u | RS2=U | F12, 2.1.2 step 2, about every model
Rule 1. Every proposal must not proceed, if that proposal is external, unless that proposal is classified as "governance_found_acceptable".
## f13-p | RS2=P | F13, 3.1.2 step 2, within the process for models reaching an ML R&D and misalignment T/CCL
Rule 1. Every proposal must not proceed, if all of the following hold: (a) either that proposal is external or that proposal is classified as "high_risk", or both; (b) there is a level such that both that proposal has reached that level and that level is classified as "ml_rd_and_misalignment", unless that proposal is classified as "governance_found_acceptable".
## f13-u | RS2=U | F13, 3.1.2 step 2, about every model
Rule 1. Every proposal must not proceed, if either that proposal is external or that proposal is classified as "high_risk", or both, unless that proposal is classified as "governance_found_acceptable".
## f14 | always | F14, 2.1.2 and 3.1.2 step 3 "Material updates to a safety case will be submitted to the appropriate governance function for review"
Rule 1. Every proposal must be submitted to review by the appropriate governance function, if that proposal is classified as "material_safety_case_update".
## f15-same | RS6=same | F15, 2.2 "additional mitigations beyond these established safeguards are not required"; RS6 same: the SL2+ insider-threat measures
Rule 1. Every proposal need not apply each measure to the model weights, if all of the following hold: (a) there is a level such that both that proposal has reached that level and that level is misuse; (b) that measure addresses insiders.
## f15-diff | RS6=different | F15, 2.2: insider misuse is not insider threat to weights
Rule 1. Every proposal need not add mitigations against insider misuse beyond the baseline controls, if there is a level such that both that proposal has reached that level and that level is misuse.
## f16-ds | RS3=Ds | F16, 2.1.1, 2.2, 3.2.2 and footnote 11: the field's "should", read distributively, default force (N2)
Rule 1. Every proposal should apply each measure to the model weights, if there is a level such that all of the following hold: (a) that proposal has reached that level; (b) at least one of the following holds: (i) that level recommends that measure; (ii) there is a second measure such that both that level recommends the second measure and the second measure includes that measure. Rule 1 is excepted when at least one of the following holds: (a) that proposal is classified as "like_public_models"; (b) either that proposal is classified as "security_assessed_adequate" or that proposal is classified as "open_release_benefits_outweigh_risks", or both. The exception to rule 1 is decided by the developer.
## f17-pra | always | F17, 3.2.1 "When a model has reached this TCL, we will carry out periodic residual risk assessments of the misalignment risk posed"
Rule 1. Every proposal must be subject to periodic residual risk assessments of misalignment risk, if there is a level such that all of the following hold: (a) that proposal has reached that level; (b) both that level is tracked and that level is classified as "ml_rd_and_misalignment".
## f17-add | always | F17, 3.2.1 "If the risk assessment deems the residual risk from internal deployment to be unacceptable without additional safeguards ..., these will be applied"
Rule 1. Every proposal must have the additional safeguards applied, if all of the following hold: (a) both that proposal is internal and that proposal is classified as "internal_risk_unacceptable_without_safeguards"; (b) there is a level such that all of the following hold: (i) that proposal has reached that level; (ii) both that level is tracked and that level is classified as "ml_rd_and_misalignment".
## f18-yearly | always | F18, 5.1 "The Frontier Safety Framework will be reviewed at least once a year"
Rule 1. Every proposal must be covered by a review of the framework at least once a year.
## f18-frequent | always | F18, 5.1 "more frequently if we have reasonable grounds to believe the adequacy of the Framework or our adherence to it has been materially undermined"
Rule 1. Every proposal must be covered by a more frequent review of the framework, if that proposal is classified as "adherence_undermined".
## f19-default | RS4aim=default | F19, 5.2 "we aim to share relevant information with appropriate government authorities", read as a default norm
Rule 1. Every proposal should share relevant information with appropriate government authorities, if all of the following hold: (a) there is a level such that both that proposal has reached that level and that level is critical; (b) both that proposal is classified as "unmitigated_public_safety_risk" and that proposal is classified as "sharing_facilitates_safety".
## f20-holistic-strict | RS4holistic=strict | F20, 1.3.5 Note "should also be assessed holistically and be proportionate with expected impact"
Rule 1. Every proposal must have its mitigations assessed holistically in proportion to expected impact.
## f20-holistic-default | RS4holistic=default | F20, 1.3.5 Note, read as a default norm
Rule 1. Every proposal should have its mitigations assessed holistically in proportion to expected impact.
## f20-within-strict | RS4within=strict | F20, Glossary "The residual risk should be brought within the acceptable levels, as determined by the T/CCLs as relevant"
Rule 1. Every proposal must have its residual risk brought within the acceptable levels, if there is a level such that that proposal has reached that level.
## f20-within-default | RS4within=default | F20, Glossary, read as a default norm
Rule 1. Every proposal should have its residual risk brought within the acceptable levels, if there is a level such that that proposal has reached that level.
## f20-elicitation-strict | RS4elicitation=strict | F20, Note on ML R&D CCLs "Risk assessment must take into account the fact that other actors may put significantly more effort into eliciting capabilities"
Rule 1. Every proposal must have its risk assessment consider greater elicitation effort by others.
## f20-elicitation-default | RS4elicitation=default | F20, Note on ML R&D CCLs, read as a default norm
Rule 1. Every proposal should have its risk assessment consider greater elicitation effort by others.
